# Line endings.
#
# The guest half of this project is Linux: bash scripts, an XKB keymap, labwc/LXQt config and
# .desktop files that are bind-mounted into the runtime's rootfs and executed there. A CRLF
# checkout breaks them in ways that look like something else entirely - bash reports
# "syntax error near unexpected token `$'\r''" and exits 2, which the app shows as
# "<name> stopped unexpectedly" - so a Windows checkout must not be able to produce one.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises every text file to LF in the repository AND in the working tree,
# whatever the machine's core.autocrlf says. Binary files are detected and left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The one genuinely Windows-only file: cmd.exe reads CRLF batch files, and gradlew.bat is
# committed with CRLF upstream.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Explicitly binary - never normalise, never diff as text. `text=auto` already detects most of
# these, but naming them keeps a future checkout from guessing wrong about an asset whose bytes
# are the deliverable (the driver bundles, the fonts, the startup movie).
*.tzst binary
*.so binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webm binary
*.ttf binary
*.p12 binary
*.jar binary
*.dex binary
